  "output" : "I've read the context and explored the repo. Here's my understanding:\n\n**openloop** — a Swift-based AI agent orchestrator (SwiftPM monorepo, macOS 14+ / iOS 16+) with these targets in `Package.swift`:\n\n| Target | Role |\n|---|---|\n| `openloop` | CLI executable |\n| `runner` | Workflow execution engine (uses `llm-graph` for agent graphs) |\n| `api` | **Vapor web service** — web UI + REST API for controlling/monitoring workflows & operations |\n| `w2` | Utility executable |\n| `shared` | Shared library (DB via SQLite.swift, model, launcher, notifications, workflow validation, etc.) |\n\n**The `api` service** specifically:\n- Auto-registers itself as a launchd background service (`openloop-api` on port **54321**) so it survives reboots\n- Serves a static web UI from `Sources/api/Public/` (`index.html`, `graph.html`, `workflow-log.html`, `notifications.html`, panel CSS/JS, plus `llms.txt`/docs for agent consumption)\n- Exposes a REST API under `/api/instances/...` with handlers for:\n  - **Instances** — launch/stop/disable/unload/delete\n  - **Workflows** — CRUD + runs listing\n  - **Personas** — CRUD (the \"AI teammate\" role definitions)\n  - Plus **Logs**, **Graphs**, **Knowledge**, **Manual workflows**, **Notifications** handlers\n- Agents it orchestrates: `claude-code`, `opencode`, `mistral-vibe` (opencode has OOM issues on Linux per the README)\n\nWhat would you like me to do — investigate something in `api`, add a feature, fix a bug, review code, or something else?\n"
